WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:04.504
-Hello, everyone, and welcome
back to my attic crawl space.

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.138
Of course now that we've shifted

00:00:06.138 --> 00:00:08.641
our makeshift studio
to this location,

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:11.077
there's one question that has
preoccupied our audience

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:14.146
perhaps more than any other
and that's, "What's up...

00:00:14.146 --> 00:00:17.016
What's up with that
tiny little door over there?"

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:19.385
I mean, is it where
we keep the kids' toys?

00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:21.454
Or is it a Wonka door?

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:24.124
And if it's a Wonka door,
is the tiny chair --

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:26.826
right there --
is that for an Oompa Loompa,

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.428
waiting to roll me away
to the juicing room

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:30.095
after eating
an everlasting gobstopper?

00:00:30.095 --> 00:00:31.331
Who knows?

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:33.499
The only thing I know
is that I'll never tell.

00:00:33.499 --> 00:00:35.634
Anyway, you'll have
plenty of time to speculate

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:38.037
because we'll be doing these
"Closer Looks" here for a while.

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:40.039
Public health officials
are urging Americans

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:42.741
to continue observing
social distancing rules

00:00:42.741 --> 00:00:44.644
even as the president
and his son-in-law

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:46.646
contradict those experts

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:48.347
and spread
dangerous misinformation.

00:00:48.347 --> 00:00:50.483
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:54.220
♪♪

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:57.924
Well, we're less than
a week into the month of April.

00:00:57.924 --> 00:01:00.526
There's really no way
of knowing what day it is.

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:02.295
Every day is a week
and every week is a year

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:05.431
and now April just means --
I don't know -- Tuesday?

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:06.633
The calendar app on my phone

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:10.069
is just a shrug emoji
holding a glass of wine.

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:13.305
But if it is, in fact, April,
then that's great news,

00:01:13.305 --> 00:01:14.940
because if you remember,

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:16.843
when public health officials
were first warning

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:18.777
about the coming outbreak
of the coronavirus,

00:01:18.777 --> 00:01:22.248
the President reassured us all
by saying this.

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:24.984
-The virus.
They're working hard.

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:26.986
Looks like, by April,
you know, in theory,

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:30.089
when it gets a little warmer,
it miraculously goes away.

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:31.390
I hope that's true.

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:34.794
Now, the virus that we're
talking about having to do,

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:37.397
you know, a lot of people think
that goes away in April

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:39.832
with the heat,
as the heat comes in.

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:41.868
Typically,
that will go away in April.

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:43.403
We're in great shape, though.

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:45.105
-President Xi --
I know you spoke to him

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:47.740
recently about coronavirus.
-I did.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.709
-Some concerns
that their economy

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:52.711
is really going to tank
because of this,

00:01:52.711 --> 00:01:55.314
and that that could have
a spillover effect here.

00:01:55.314 --> 00:01:58.050
What's your sense of
their transparency right now,

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:00.319
whether they're being
more accommodating in terms

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:03.323
of telling us what's going on,
and how it affects our economy?

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:06.392
-Well, I think China is very,
you know, professionally run

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:08.661
in the sense that they
have everything under control.

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:10.162
I really believe they are going
to have it

00:02:10.162 --> 00:02:11.864
under control fairly soon.

00:02:11.864 --> 00:02:15.268
You know, in April, supposedly,
it dies with the hotter weather.

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:17.069
And that's a beautiful date
to look forward to.

00:02:17.069 --> 00:02:18.871
-First of all,
you can tell my man

00:02:18.871 --> 00:02:20.640
spends too much time
at Mar-A-Lago

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:24.043
because he thinks April
is when it gets hot.

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:27.012
"In February, the trees begin
to bloom, and by April,

00:02:27.012 --> 00:02:30.182
I mean, you can barely touch
your steering wheel."

00:02:30.182 --> 00:02:32.551
But, yes, it's a beautiful day
to look forward to.

00:02:32.551 --> 00:02:33.919
I remember when we all got

00:02:33.919 --> 00:02:36.222
that lovely save-the-date
in the mail.

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:38.290
By the way, the anchor who
conducted that last interview

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:40.927
was since fired Fox Business
host Trish Regan

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:43.162
who called coronavirus
an impeachment scam.

00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:46.165
Remember her?
Evil Connie Britton?

00:02:46.165 --> 00:02:47.400
"Friday Night Lights"

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.135
would have been a totally
different show with her.

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:51.504
"Your team sucks, coach,
and so do you.

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:54.240
Also, it's high school football.
Who cares?

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.374
You know what I say?

00:02:55.374 --> 00:02:58.411
'Dumb eyes,
fat hearts can lose.'

00:03:03.282 --> 00:03:05.818
I'm outta wine."

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:08.020
But credit to Fox News
who will not hesitate to fire

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:10.623
a host who peddles
dangerous conspiracy theories

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:13.492
as long as they're not
Sean Insanity.

00:03:13.492 --> 00:03:15.794
Because Hannity will probably
end his show tonight

00:03:15.794 --> 00:03:17.496
telling people
that snorting Advil

00:03:17.496 --> 00:03:21.201
is both a cure for coronavirus
and erectile dysfunction.

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:22.602
And after that they'll
give him a raise.

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:24.469
"Great stuff
with the Advil tonight, Sean.

00:03:24.469 --> 00:03:25.804
Where'd it come from?"

00:03:25.804 --> 00:03:28.107
"Would you believe
I pulled it out of my ass?"

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:30.343
"That ass of yours, Sean,
it is a --

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:32.444
it is a bottomless gold mine.

00:03:32.444 --> 00:03:34.380
Keep up the great work."

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.749
Now, in the time Trump
was dismissing the virus

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:38.184
and claiming it would go away,

00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:40.386
he was repeatedly warned
by intelligence briefings

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:42.255
that this was a real threat.

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:43.623
And in that time,
"The Washington Post"

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:46.458
reported his administration
was beset by 70 days

00:03:46.458 --> 00:03:48.594
of denial,
delays, and dysfunction.

00:03:48.594 --> 00:03:50.229
70 days.

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:52.265
And that's charitable, because
for Trump, you could say

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:55.067
it's been
70 years of dysfunction.

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:57.302
When he was born, the doctor
spanked him on the butt

00:03:57.302 --> 00:03:59.171
to hear him cry, and instead,
Trump called him nasty

00:03:59.171 --> 00:04:00.906
and served him with a lawsuit.

00:04:00.906 --> 00:04:03.409
"There's an expression I use --
'wah.'

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:05.945
Some people say I invented it."

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:07.146
That's baby Trump.

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:10.450
In a normal world, a story about
a 70-day delay

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:12.818
in the face of a pandemic
would be cause

00:04:12.818 --> 00:04:14.553
for impeachment or removal or,

00:04:14.553 --> 00:04:16.155
at the very least,
embarrassment and shame.

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:20.259
But the President insisted that
April would be the magic date

00:04:20.259 --> 00:04:22.795
so we could all
just look forward to that.

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:25.031
So let's check in
on his daily mini-MAGA

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:26.866
rally in the White House
briefing room on Saturday

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:29.035
to see how that prediction
is working out.

00:04:29.035 --> 00:04:30.903
-This will be probably
the toughest week

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.972
between this week and next week.

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:35.742
And there will be
a lot of death, unfortunately.

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:39.545
But a lot less death
than if this wasn't done.

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:40.545
But there will be death.

00:04:40.545 --> 00:04:43.148
-There will be death?

00:04:43.148 --> 00:04:44.650
That's kind of a 180.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:46.185
Everything was going to be fine,
and now you sound

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:47.787
like the captain
of the wrestling team

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:50.322
who just saw a nerd dancing
with his girlfriend.

00:04:50.322 --> 00:04:51.957
"There will be death."

00:04:51.957 --> 00:04:55.795
[ Grunts ]
It's a beer can.

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:57.563
What happened to April?

00:04:57.563 --> 00:05:00.265
"It's become clear now
that the end date

00:05:00.265 --> 00:05:04.303
we had been promised was,
in fact, an April Fool's joke

00:05:04.303 --> 00:05:05.671
pulled on us by the virus.

00:05:05.671 --> 00:05:09.107
So now we know corona to be
both highly contagious

00:05:09.107 --> 00:05:11.276
as well
as mischievous in spirit.

00:05:11.276 --> 00:05:14.747
A Loki, if you will."

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:16.348
Now, you might hear
that new tone and think,

00:05:16.348 --> 00:05:18.251
"Oh, I guess the President,
like any decent human being,

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:20.953
has admitted he was wrong,
made amends by doing everything

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:23.022
he can to rectify
the situation, and apologized."

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:24.390
And if you are thinking that,

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:27.927
congratulations on waking up
from your 3 1/2 year coma,

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:29.862
but bad news -- there's this
thing called coronavirus.

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:31.096
Anyway, your doctor
will tell you.

00:05:31.096 --> 00:05:34.166
Because, as usual, Trump
insisted that he was right

00:05:34.166 --> 00:05:36.235
when he said the virus
would simply go away.

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:39.004
-You look at those individual
statements, they're all true.

00:05:39.004 --> 00:05:40.105
Stay calm.

00:05:40.105 --> 00:05:41.607
Uh, it will go away.

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:43.943
You know --
You know it is going away.

00:05:43.943 --> 00:05:45.311
And it will go away.

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:48.214
-The President was saying
this was going to go away.

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:50.048
It's April.
-It is going to go away.

00:05:50.048 --> 00:05:51.684
-But, Mr. President,
you said it was going to

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:54.520
go away in April.
-I didn't say a date.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:56.755
-I said it's going away,
and it is going away.

00:05:56.755 --> 00:05:59.392
-Ah, yes, very clever.

00:05:59.392 --> 00:06:01.626
After all,
April as 24 days left,

00:06:01.626 --> 00:06:03.095
and it's already down to,

00:06:03.095 --> 00:06:07.466
what -- I don't know --
337,000 cases.

00:06:07.466 --> 00:06:08.801
And you did.

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:11.504
You literally said
it goes away in April.

00:06:11.504 --> 00:06:14.273
That's as close to specific
as Trump ever gets.

00:06:14.273 --> 00:06:15.674
Usually when you ask him
a question,

00:06:15.674 --> 00:06:17.910
he waves it away like a dad
promising his kids

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:20.179
a trip to Disneyland
while watching football.

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:22.414
"Dad, will we have
universal healthcare?"

00:06:22.414 --> 00:06:25.250
"Yeah, it's going to be so easy,
it's going to be a blast.

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:28.654
Now go upstairs and oil
your hair before dinner."

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:30.990
And then, last week,
the media fell for his fake

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:32.558
somber Trump shtick

00:06:32.558 --> 00:06:35.093
and asked him
if his thinking had changed from

00:06:35.093 --> 00:06:37.996
when he said the virus
would go away in April.

00:06:37.996 --> 00:06:39.932
-Is there any fairness
to the criticism

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:41.801
that you may have
lulled Americans

00:06:41.801 --> 00:06:44.803
into a false sense of security
when you were saying things like

00:06:44.803 --> 00:06:46.505
it's going to go away...
-Well, it is.

00:06:46.505 --> 00:06:48.340
-...and that sort of thing.
-Jim, it's going away.

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:49.808
-But when you were saying --
-It's going to go away.

00:06:49.808 --> 00:06:51.911
Hopefully at the end
of the month and if not,

00:06:51.911 --> 00:06:53.679
it hopefully
will be soon after that.

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:55.314
-But --
-So it is going away.

00:06:55.314 --> 00:06:56.816
-Has your thinking
on this evolved?

00:06:56.816 --> 00:06:57.816
-It is going away.

00:06:57.816 --> 00:06:59.618
-Has your thinking
on this evolved?

00:06:59.618 --> 00:07:01.520
You're taking it
more seriously now?

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:05.257
-I think, from the beginning,
my attitude was that

00:07:05.257 --> 00:07:07.459
we have to give this country --
I know how bad it was.

00:07:07.459 --> 00:07:09.595
All you have to do is look
at what was going on in China.

00:07:09.595 --> 00:07:13.365
-First of all, no,
you didn't know how bad it was.

00:07:13.365 --> 00:07:15.134
You treated coronavirus
like a [bleep]

00:07:15.134 --> 00:07:17.035
high school baseball coach
talking to a kid

00:07:17.035 --> 00:07:19.405
who just got hit
by a line drive to the head.

00:07:19.405 --> 00:07:21.006
"How many fingers
am I holding up?"

00:07:21.006 --> 00:07:22.174
"I don't know. 50?"

00:07:22.174 --> 00:07:26.745
"He's good to go!
Get him back in there."

00:07:26.745 --> 00:07:28.413
Of course his thinking
hasn't evolved.

00:07:28.413 --> 00:07:30.583
He's barely evolved.
I mean, look at him,

00:07:30.583 --> 00:07:32.552
he looks like
one of those early tetrapods

00:07:32.552 --> 00:07:35.153
that crawled out of the water
and learned how to walk on land,

00:07:35.153 --> 00:07:37.022
but then he didn't learn
how to hunt or fish

00:07:37.022 --> 00:07:39.124
so he ended up
just walking around

00:07:39.124 --> 00:07:41.894
in circles like a dude
waiting for a crosstown bus.

00:07:41.894 --> 00:07:45.297
"Anyone know
when the M15 is coming?

00:07:45.297 --> 00:07:47.399
Canceled?
Why?

00:07:47.399 --> 00:07:48.734
Because of coronavirus?

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:51.437
But it's April."

00:07:51.437 --> 00:07:53.572
So Trump insists he was right
when he said it would go away

00:07:53.572 --> 00:07:55.274
possibly
by the end of this month.

00:07:55.274 --> 00:07:57.009
Now, you could
either believe him

00:07:57.009 --> 00:07:59.945
or you could believe Bill Gates.

00:07:59.945 --> 00:08:02.148
-Well, this is
a nightmare scenario

00:08:02.148 --> 00:08:04.950
because human-to-human
transmissible

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:08.554
respiratory viruses
can grow exponentially.

00:08:08.554 --> 00:08:13.158
We continue countrywide, and
we're testing the right people

00:08:13.158 --> 00:08:16.462
to understand what's going on,
which is not the case yet,

00:08:16.462 --> 00:08:18.764
those numbers
will start to go down.

00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:22.835
And then, we can look at
some degree of opening back up.

00:08:22.835 --> 00:08:27.606
Things won't go back to truly
normal until we have a vaccine

00:08:27.606 --> 00:08:30.976
that we've gotten out
to basically the entire world.

00:08:30.976 --> 00:08:33.145
-So there you go.
Who are you going to believe,

00:08:33.145 --> 00:08:35.680
the pioneer
of the microcomputer revolution

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:37.116
who founded Microsoft

00:08:37.116 --> 00:08:40.319
and is currently working
on ending polio and malaria?

00:08:40.319 --> 00:08:42.220
Or the guy who once tweeted,

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:44.924
"Victoria's Secret reps
were nasty to Kate Upton,

00:08:44.924 --> 00:08:47.025
and now she's doing great."

00:08:47.025 --> 00:08:48.260
That tweet was from 2013,

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:49.962
and while I don't know
what it's about,

00:08:49.962 --> 00:08:52.197
I am genuinely,
genuinely curious,

00:08:52.197 --> 00:08:54.533
and I intend to do some Google
investigating as soon as this

00:08:54.533 --> 00:08:57.269
[bleep] pandemic is over.

00:08:57.269 --> 00:08:59.205
Also, why were you
commenting on that?

00:08:59.205 --> 00:09:01.274
Is that what you used to spend
your time on

00:09:01.274 --> 00:09:02.541
before you became president?

00:09:02.541 --> 00:09:04.610
"Mr. Trump, we're ready to shoot
'The Apprentice.'"

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:09.815
"Yeah, quiet. I'm taking sides
in Upton v. Secret."

00:09:09.815 --> 00:09:11.750
And now in part
because the president

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:13.285
waved away
the problem for 70 days,

00:09:13.285 --> 00:09:15.988
we're facing both
an unimaginable tragedy

00:09:15.988 --> 00:09:17.990
and also an economic collapse

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:20.459
that has already resulted
in the worst weekly jobless

00:09:20.459 --> 00:09:23.028
claims numbers we've ever seen,
and yet Americans

00:09:23.028 --> 00:09:25.898
are still having trouble
accessing government benefits.

00:09:25.898 --> 00:09:27.933
Just take this story
from "The New York Times"

00:09:27.933 --> 00:09:30.502
about one applicant
who saw jobless benefits

00:09:30.502 --> 00:09:33.639
and was told to find
a fax machine.

00:09:33.639 --> 00:09:35.541
Some attempts to apply
for benefits

00:09:35.541 --> 00:09:39.378
yielded a pop-up message
that suggested using Netscape,

00:09:39.378 --> 00:09:41.814
a browser that effectively
no longer exists.

00:09:41.814 --> 00:09:43.849
One applicant said he was
taken aback to hear

00:09:43.849 --> 00:09:46.885
he had to find a fax machine
to complete his claim.

00:09:46.885 --> 00:09:49.888
My God, it's 2020,
in the richest country on Earth,

00:09:49.888 --> 00:09:52.090
but if you need government
benefits you have to go

00:09:52.090 --> 00:09:54.260
on an early '90s treasure hunt.

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:55.794
"Hey, guys, I found a clue.

00:09:55.794 --> 00:10:01.133
If financial aid you wish to
get, find yourself a Giga Pet."

00:10:01.133 --> 00:10:03.602
They have to use Netscape
and fax machines.

00:10:03.602 --> 00:10:05.804
What if they want
to apply in person?

00:10:05.804 --> 00:10:07.706
Do they have to go
to a Hollywood Video?

00:10:07.706 --> 00:10:09.942
"Great. Okay.
Thank you for this.

00:10:09.942 --> 00:10:12.244
Now, the last thing you need
to do before you collect

00:10:12.244 --> 00:10:16.015
your benefits is watch
this VHS copy of 'Gremlins.'

00:10:16.015 --> 00:10:18.217
That will be followed
by a short quiz just so,

00:10:18.217 --> 00:10:20.218
you know, we're sure
you understand the Gremlin rules

00:10:20.218 --> 00:10:21.920
in regards to, you know,
sunlight and water,

00:10:21.920 --> 00:10:24.356
you know, when is
a safe time to feed them."

00:10:24.356 --> 00:10:26.558
That's a "Gremlin" bit
that I would not have done

